---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { DONATE_URL } from '../consts.js';
---
<Base
  title="The Philippines Vision | Send Josh — Josh Montague, Training Leaders International"
  description="A new three-year training partnership in the Philippines: sixteen pastors, nine trips, and a vision for trained men training men."
  path="/philippines/"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width:820px;">
      <p class="eyebrow">The vision</p>
      <h1>The Philippines, and beyond.</h1>
      <p style="font-size:1.15rem;">A new partnership is forming in the province of Cavite: sixteen pastors, nine training trips, three years. Further partnerships are being considered on the islands of Cebu, Mindanao, and Mindoro. And the pattern behind it has already been proven.</p>
      <p style="margin:28px 0 0;"><a class="btn-donate" href={DONATE_URL}>Donate</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-rule section-panel">
    <div class="wrap grid-2">
      <div class="photo">
        <img src="/images/philippines-cohort.jpg" alt="Filipino pastors gathered for training at Redeemer Hall" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Why the Philippines</p>
        <p>The church in the Philippines is growing far faster than its pastors can be trained. Most of the men shepherding these congregations will never have access to a seminary &mdash; not because they lack the desire or the gifts, but because the schools, the books, and the teachers simply aren't there.</p>
        <p>Josh has already taught extensively in the Philippines &mdash; hermeneutics, biblical theology, Old Testament narrative, the Gospels, the Psalms, Ephesians, Isaiah. The new partnership turns those individual trips into a sustained, sequential program.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-rule">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">The plan for 2027</p>
      <h2>Sixteen pastors. Nine trips. Three years.</h2>
      <div class="grid-3" style="margin-top:36px;">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">01</p>
          <h3>A cohort, not a conference</h3>
          <p style="font-size:0.98rem;">Sixteen Filipino pastors, walking together through a multi-year curriculum that covers the whole counsel of God &mdash; how to understand the Scriptures, and how to preach them.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">02</p>
          <h3>Nine trips over three years</h3>
          <p style="font-size:0.98rem;">Roughly three training trips a year, each building on the last. Between trips, the pastors put the training to work in their own pulpits and report back.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">03</p>
          <h3>Trained men training men</h3>
          <p style="font-size:0.98rem;">Every pastor in the cohort is urged to pass the training on to others. The aim is a multiplying movement of expository preaching that outlasts the trips themselves.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-rule">
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width:820px;">
      <p class="eyebrow">A new venture</p>
      <h2>Reaching the island of Mindoro.</h2>
      <p>While only a few hours away from the bustle of Manila, the island of Mindoro feels like a different world. While pastors around Manila generally have access to training and resources, those on Mindoro do not. Stemming from his doctoral work exploring training among oral cultures, Josh plans on launching training on Mindoro in partnership with Filipino graduates of previous cohorts. This new work, starting in 2027, will pioneer methods and approaches that will help TLI and its partners train in new regions of the world.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-rule section-panel">
    <div class="wrap grid-2">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">A proven pattern</p>
        <h2>This has worked before.</h2>
        <p>Over the past eight years, Josh coordinated training for ten Pakistani pastors &mdash; men who could not be reached in their own country, so the training met them in Dubai and Amman. Today, six of those pastors continue to work with Josh monthly as they move through the ordination process.</p>
        <p>While Josh's work has focused on Pakistanis and Filipinos over the last five years, TLI has graduated dozens of cohorts around the world.</p>
        <p>The Philippines partnership applies the same patient, relational model &mdash; and partnerships beyond it are already being explored in Africa and Asia.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="photo">
        <img src="/images/josh-whiteboard-teaching.jpg" alt="Josh teaching the Bible's storyline to pastors" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-rule">
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width:760px;">
      <p class="eyebrow">From a trainee</p>
      <!-- TODO: Josh will send a testimony from a trainee — insert quote + attribution here -->
      <blockquote style="color:var(--muted);">A testimony from one of Josh's trainees will appear here soon.</blockquote>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-rule">
    <div class="wrap" style="text-align:center; max-width:760px;">
      <h2 class="caps-head">Pray for the work</h2>
      <p style="font-size:1.05rem;">Please pray for wisdom, and for the provision of funds and teachers. Then consider whether your church might share in the work itself.</p>
      <a class="btn-dark" href="/support/" style="margin-top:16px;">See the need</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
